---
/**
 * /terms/ — Terms of Service.
 *
 * Plain-English commercial terms for an Australian B2B electronic security
 * installer. Drafted to cover the standard ground (engagement, payment,
 * warranty, IP, liability, dispute resolution, governing law) without
 * lawyer-speak. Karl/Lesley should still have legal counsel review before
 * any meaningful change is made.
 *
 * Brand voice notes carried through: plain English, no jargon-as-decoration,
 * no em dashes. Mirrors the structure of the Privacy Policy for consistency.
 */
import LegalLayout from '@layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@lib/site';

const seo = {
  title: 'Terms of Service',
  description: `Terms of service for ${site.legalName}, commercial electronic security solutions in Sydney.`,
  path: '/terms/',
};
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  intro={`These terms govern use of this website and any commercial engagement between you and ${site.legalName}. They are written in plain English so the meaning is clear before you sign anything.`}
  lastUpdated="Last updated: April 2026"
  seo={seo}
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}, trading as Ktronics Electronic Security Solutions, is a
    Sydney-based commercial electronic security business operating under
    NSW Master Licence <strong>{site.credentials.nswMasterLicence}</strong>
    and ASIAL Gold membership. We design, install, monitor, and maintain
    access control, intercoms, alarms, video surveillance, and integrated
    security systems for Australian businesses.
  </p>
  <p>
    In these terms, "Ktronics", "we", "us", and "our" refer to
    {' '}{site.legalName}. "You" refers to the business or person engaging
    Ktronics for services or using this website.
  </p>

  <h2>2. About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply in two ways. First, they govern your use of this
    website. Second, they form the baseline for any commercial engagement
    you enter into with Ktronics. If we issue you a quote, work order,
    service contract, or other written agreement, that document takes
    precedence over these terms wherever the two are inconsistent.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date
    at the top reflects the most recent change. Continued use of the
    website after a change indicates acceptance of the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Use of this website</h2>
  <p>
    The content on this website is published in good faith for general
    information. It is not advice tailored to your site, your sector, or
    your compliance obligations. Pricing ranges, retention recommendations,
    and capability descriptions are indicative; the right specification
    for your business comes out of a site walk-through and a written
    quote, not the website.
  </p>
  <p>
    All written content, photographs, diagrams, schemas, and code on this
    site are owned by Ktronics or used with permission. You may view,
    print, and forward our content for non-commercial business research
    purposes. You may not republish, sell, modify, or systematically
    extract content without our written consent.
  </p>
  <p>
    The website may link to third-party sites (manufacturer pages,
    industry bodies, professional resources). Those links are provided as
    a convenience. We are not responsible for the content, accuracy,
    practices, or policies of third-party sites.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Quotes and engagement of services</h2>
  <p>
    A quote from Ktronics is an offer to provide the scope of work described
    in that quote, valid for the period stated on the quote (typically 30
    days from issue). A quote becomes a contract once you accept it in
    writing (signed acceptance, purchase order, or written confirmation by
    email).
  </p>
  <p>
    The contract between us is made up of: the accepted quote, any
    associated specifications and drawings, our written service or
    maintenance agreement (where applicable), and these terms. Where any
    of these documents conflict, the order above is the order of
    precedence (accepted quote first, these terms last).
  </p>
  <p>
    Variations to the agreed scope (for example: additional doors, extra
    cameras, change of cabling pathway, change of head-end equipment) will
    be quoted separately in writing before the work is performed. We will
    not proceed with variations that materially change cost or timeline
    without your written approval.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Payment terms</h2>
  <p>
    Unless otherwise agreed in writing on the quote, our standard payment
    terms are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>A deposit of 30% of the quoted price on acceptance of the quote, before equipment is ordered.</li>
    <li>Progress claims at agreed milestones for projects over $20,000.</li>
    <li>Final invoice on practical completion, payable within 14 days.</li>
    <li>Service and maintenance contract fees billed monthly or annually in advance.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Overdue invoices may attract interest at 2% per month (or part thereof)
    on the outstanding balance, calculated daily. Recovery costs we incur
    in collecting overdue amounts are payable by you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Title to equipment supplied by us does not pass to you until the
    related invoice is paid in full. We retain a security interest in
    unpaid equipment under the Personal Property Securities Act 2009 (Cth)
    and may register that interest on the PPSR.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Workmanship and equipment warranty</h2>
  <p>
    We warrant that work performed by Ktronics technicians will be carried
    out with reasonable skill and care, in accordance with the relevant
    Australian Standards, and to the requirements of the NSW Security
    Industry Act 1997. Defects in our workmanship reported within 12
    months of practical completion will be rectified at no charge.
  </p>
  <p>
    Equipment we supply carries the manufacturer's warranty (typically
    one to three years, varying by product). We will support warranty
    claims with the manufacturer on your behalf and replace or repair
    defective equipment in line with the manufacturer's terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    Warranty does not cover: damage caused by misuse, modification by
    third parties, power surges, lightning, water damage outside the
    equipment's rated environment, force majeure events, or normal wear
    and tear of consumable items (batteries, lamps, cleaning materials).
  </p>

  <h2>7. Service and response times</h2>
  <p>
    Where you have an active service or maintenance contract with us,
    response times are governed by that contract. Standard response times
    referenced on this website (for example, "next business day" or "4
    hours") are guidelines and only become contractual commitments when
    written into a signed agreement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Emergency response (for sites with monitored alarm panels) operates
    around the clock through our 24/7 monitoring control room on
    {' '}<a href={`tel:${site.contact.emergencyPhoneTel}`}>{site.contact.emergencyPhone}</a>.
    Emergency call-out fees and after-hours rates apply where the
    contract does not include them.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Site access and your obligations</h2>
  <p>
    To deliver our services, we need: safe and timely access to the work
    areas, accurate information about the building (including known
    hazards), nominated points of contact authorised to make decisions on
    your behalf, and reasonable cooperation with any compliance, safety,
    or operational protocols we propose.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delays caused by site access issues, late information, or unapproved
    variations may attract additional charges. We will notify you in
    writing before charging for delay-related costs.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Designs, drawings, schedules, specifications, and configuration files
    we produce in the course of an engagement remain the intellectual
    property of Ktronics. Once your invoice is paid in full, you receive
    a perpetual, royalty-free licence to use those materials for the
    purpose of operating, maintaining, and updating the security system
    we delivered.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where you supply us with information (floor plans, asset registers,
    cardholder lists, operational procedures), that information remains
    yours. We will only use it to deliver the services you engage us
    for, and we handle it in accordance with our
    {' '}<a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>
    Both parties will treat the other's commercial, technical, and
    operational information as confidential and will not disclose it to
    third parties without consent, except where required by law,
    regulator, or in the course of delivering the engaged services
    (for example, to a manufacturer for a warranty claim).
  </p>
  <p>
    Ktronics does not publish client names without written permission.
    Anonymised case studies sometimes describe sectors, scope, and
    outcomes for marketing purposes; client-identifying information is
    withheld unless you specifically authorise it in writing.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts, or modifies any rights or
    remedies you have under the Australian Consumer Law (Schedule 2 of
    the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth)) or any other law that
    cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>
  <p>
    Subject to the paragraph above, our total liability to you for any
    claim arising out of or in connection with the services (whether in
    contract, tort, statute, or otherwise) is limited at our option to:
    re-supply of the relevant services, payment of the cost of having the
    relevant services re-supplied, or a refund of the amount paid for the
    relevant services. In no case will our total aggregate liability
    exceed the amount you have paid us under the relevant engagement in
    the 12 months preceding the claim.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are not liable for indirect, consequential, or special losses,
    including loss of profit, revenue, business opportunity, data, or
    goodwill, even if those losses were foreseeable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Electronic security systems reduce risk; they do not eliminate it.
    No installer can guarantee that an alarm will always activate, that
    a camera will always capture usable footage, that monitored response
    will always prevent loss, or that a system will never be defeated by
    a determined attacker. You acknowledge this in engaging us.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Insurance</h2>
  <p>
    Ktronics holds public liability insurance, professional indemnity
    insurance, and product liability insurance to industry-standard
    levels. Certificates of currency are available on request.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    Either party may terminate a service or maintenance contract by
    giving the notice period specified in that contract (typically 30
    days). Where no notice period is specified, 30 days written notice
    applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Either party may terminate immediately if the other materially
    breaches these terms or the underlying contract and fails to remedy
    the breach within 14 days of written notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    On termination, you remain liable for: amounts invoiced and unpaid
    at the date of termination, work performed and equipment supplied
    up to that date, and any non-cancellable supplier commitments we
    have made on your behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Personal information collected through this website or in the course
    of providing services is handled in accordance with our
    {' '}<a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Where we install or
    monitor systems that capture personal information about people on
    your site (cardholders, visitors, footage subjects), the operator of
    the site is the data controller; we act on your behalf and in line
    with the contract.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Force majeure</h2>
  <p>
    Neither party is liable for failure or delay in performing
    obligations caused by events beyond reasonable control, including:
    natural disasters, pandemics, government action, industrial action,
    failure of utilities, supplier default, or cyber incidents. The
    affected party will notify the other promptly and will use
    reasonable efforts to resume performance.
  </p>

  <h2>16. Dispute resolution</h2>
  <p>
    If a dispute arises, both parties agree to first try to resolve it
    through good-faith negotiation. If that fails within 30 days, the
    parties will attempt mediation through the Resolution Institute
    (resolution.institute) before commencing court proceedings, except
    where urgent injunctive relief is required.
  </p>

  <h2>17. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia.
    The parties submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of
    New South Wales and the relevant federal courts.
  </p>

  <h2>18. General</h2>
  <p>
    If any part of these terms is found to be unenforceable, that part
    will be severed and the remaining terms will continue to apply. A
    failure or delay by either party in exercising a right does not
    constitute a waiver of that right. These terms (together with any
    accepted quote, signed agreement, and our Privacy Policy) constitute
    the entire agreement between the parties relating to the subject
    matter and supersede any prior representations.
  </p>

  <h2>19. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? Contact us:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>{site.legalName}</strong><br />
    {site.address.streetAddress}<br />
    {site.address.locality} {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.contact.phoneTel}`}>{site.contact.phone}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
